For an object $X$ of a <braided monoidal category>, take its self-<braiding>
$$
\boxed{y=c_{X,X}:X\otimes X\longrightarrow X\otimes X.}
$$
It is invertible by definition. Suppress canonical <associators> using the <monoidal coherence theorem>, and put $R_{12}=y\otimes1$, $R_{23}=1\otimes y$. The hexagon identity gives
$$
c_{X,X\otimes X}=R_{23}R_{12}.
$$
Apply <naturality> of this <braiding> to the morphism $y:X\otimes X\to X\otimes X$ in its second argument. It says
$$
c_{X,X\otimes X}(1\otimes y)=(y\otimes1)c_{X,X\otimes X}.
$$
Substitution gives
$$
\boxed{R_{23}R_{12}R_{23}=R_{12}R_{23}R_{12}.}
$$
This is the equation for a <Yang–Baxter operator>. Restoring the uniquely determined <associators> gives the non-strict diagram in the paper. **Every object therefore has the canonical Yang–Baxter operator supplied by its self-braiding.**

= ii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

The <braid group> $B_n$ has generators $\sigma_1,\ldots,\sigma_{n-1}$ and relations
$$
\sigma_i\sigma_j=\sigma_j\sigma_i\ (|i-j|>1),\qquad\sigma_i\sigma_{i+1}\sigma_i=\sigma_{i+1}\sigma_i\sigma_{i+1}.
$$
In the <strict monoidal category> $\mathcal C$, put $X^{\otimes0}=I$ and send
$$
\boxed{n\longmapsto X^{\otimes n},\qquad\sigma_i\longmapsto1_X^{\otimes(i-1)}\otimes y\otimes1_X^{\otimes(n-i-1)}.}
$$
The images are invertible because the <Yang–Baxter operator> $y$ is invertible. Distant images commute by the tensor interchange law, and adjacent images satisfy the <braid group relations> by the <Yang–Baxter operator> equation tensored with the remaining identities. Thus these assignments define <group homomorphisms> $B_n\to\operatorname{Aut}(X^{\otimes n})$, and hence a <functor> $\mathbf B\to\mathcal C$.

Juxtaposition of braids puts generators into the corresponding two blocks of tensor factors, so their images are the tensor products of their images. Strictness of $\mathcal C$ gives $X^{\otimes(m+n)}=X^{\otimes m}\otimes X^{\otimes n}$ and $X^{\otimes0}=I$ exactly. **The resulting functor is strict monoidal and sends $1$ to $X$.**

= b
{parent=4}
